# Line endings: LF everywhere, on every machine, whatever core.autocrlf says.
# The repo always stored LF; Git for Windows' default (autocrlf=true) only turned the working
# copy into CRLF, which breaks tools that read raw bytes: shell scripts run on FreeBSD (MyDevil),
# and the 10x CLI, which hashes CLAUDE.md's managed block, prompts and templates byte for byte
# and reports every CRLF file as a conflict on `10x sync`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Exceptions: Windows command scripts need CRLF (cmd.exe misreads labels and jumps with LF).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never convert, never diff as text.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
